{"items":[{"recordId":"teach-generated-31acc1481df1ab2f","units":[{"role":"definition","basis":"common_knowledge","text":"An application fan is a diagram node representing the application of one function to one argument.","requires":["function application"],"citationRequired":false}]},{"recordId":"teach-generated-209163225799547c","units":[{"role":"definition","basis":"common_knowledge","text":"A function fan is a diagram node representing the function side of an application.","requires":["function application","function"],"citationRequired":false}]},{"recordId":"teach-generated-998fbadb1fba0588","units":[{"role":"definition","basis":"common_knowledge","text":"An auxiliary position is a connection point on a formal node that is not the node's principal port.","requires":["principal port","formal node"],"citationRequired":false}]},{"recordId":"teach-generated-6b1045c38008e34d","units":[{"role":"definition","basis":"common_knowledge","text":"A well-formed λ translation is a translation from a λ-calculus expression into a formal representation that preserves its abstractions, applications, variables, and binding relationships while obeying the representation's structural rules.","requires":["λ calculus","variable binding","formal representation"],"citationRequired":false}]},{"recordId":"teach-generated-74c4bd17b9109ba0","units":[{"role":"mechanism","basis":"common_knowledge","text":"An active replicator is a replicator whose principal port is connected to another agent's principal port, forming an active pair eligible for an interaction or reduction.","requires":["replicator","principal port","active pair","reduction"],"citationRequired":false}]},{"recordId":"teach-generated-c7288ddeac130052","units":[{"role":"mechanism","basis":"source","text":"Fan annihilation occurs when equal fan agents meet at their principal ports and cancel. Their corresponding auxiliary connections are exposed or reconnected according to the net's reduction rule; for fans, this interaction represents applying a λ abstraction to its argument.","requires":["fan agent","principal port","auxiliary connection","reduction rule","λ abstraction","argument"],"citationRequired":true}]},{"recordId":"teach-generated-4ded140729c2919a","units":[{"role":"definition","basis":"common_knowledge","text":"A λ abstraction is an expression that creates a function by binding a variable in a body, written λx.M. Occurrences of x in M refer to the parameter introduced by that abstraction.","requires":[],"citationRequired":false}]},{"recordId":"teach-generated-c569f81d30deecef","units":[{"role":"definition","basis":"common_knowledge","text":"An argument is the expression supplied to a function when the function is applied. In an application written M N, M is the function and N is the argument.","requires":["function application"],"citationRequired":false}]}]}
